raco-rotation-keypoints demo — NOTICE

This directory (apps/raco-rotation-keypoints/) measures keypoint repeatability
under synthetic in-plane rotation. It does not reimplement RaCo or ALIKED.

VisMatch 1.4.0 (15 October 2026), PyPI package vismatch==1.4.0:
  https://github.com/gmberton/vismatch
  https://github.com/gmberton/vismatch/releases/tag/v1.4.0
  https://pypi.org/project/vismatch/1.4.0/
  License: BSD 3-Clause
  https://github.com/gmberton/vismatch/blob/v1.4.0/LICENSE
  The wheel bundles third-party checkouts. This experiment uses
  get_matcher("raco-lightglue") and get_matcher("aliked-lightglue").
  Pinned submodule commits at tag v1.4.0:
    vismatch/third_party/RaCo      35790eb48074ed14839d0fb496b8806caa4e766b
    vismatch/third_party/LightGlue eb42fee2d71449efb0aa5c10549752b5d75384d8

RaCo: Shenoi, Lindenberger, Sarlin, and Pollefeys,
  "RaCo: Ranking and Covariance for Practical Learned Keypoints",
  3DV 2026. arXiv:2602.15755 (17 February 2026).
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.15755
  https://arxiv.org/html/2602.15755
  Code: https://github.com/cvg/RaCo (Apache-2.0)
  https://github.com/cvg/RaCo/blob/main/LICENSE
  Weights, downloaded at run time, not committed:
  https://github.com/cvg/RaCo/releases/download/v1.0.0/raco.pth
  VisMatch 1.4.0 constructs RaCo with ranker=False and
  covariance_estimator=False. The wrapper states that disabling those
  heads leaves the keypoints unchanged.

ALIKED: Zhao et al., "ALIKED: A Lighter Keypoint and Descriptor Extraction
  Network via Deformable Transformation", IEEE TIM 2023.
  https://github.com/Shiaoming/ALIKED
  The copy executed here is LightGlue's lightglue/aliked.py, whose file
  header is BSD 3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2022, Zhao Xiaoming.
  Default checkpoint, downloaded at run time, not committed:
  https://github.com/Shiaoming/ALIKED/raw/main/models/aliked-n16.pth
  This run pins model_name aliked-n16. It does not load aliked-n16rot.

LightGlue: Lindenberger, Sarlin, and Pollefeys, ICCV 2023.
  https://github.com/cvg/LightGlue (Apache-2.0)
  get_matcher also downloads the LightGlue matcher checkpoints. The
  repeatability score does not use descriptors or the matcher.

HPatches full sequences, reference frame 1.ppm only, downloaded at run
  time into work/ and not committed:
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/honggyuAn/hpatches-sequences-release
  (mirror of hpatches-sequences-release, 116 sequences)
  Dataset description repo: https://github.com/hpatches/hpatches-dataset
  (MIT). The images come from earlier sequences; the HPatches repo asks
  users to cite the original sources (Balntas et al., CVPR 2017, and the
  per-sequence notes). This demo does not relicense those photographs.

